WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.117
In a conversation, the right words are only half the answer.

00:00:04.277 --> 00:00:07.162
How should a voice change as the situation changes?

00:00:08.572 --> 00:00:15.356
Interactive TTS adapts speaking style across dialogue turns, while preserving the same speaker identity.

00:00:15.516 --> 00:00:21.057
It follows explicit requests and infers implicit cues from text, audio, and video.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:27.556
Existing context-aware TTS typically maps dialogue history to speech implicitly.

00:00:27.716 --> 00:00:33.290
Style decisions are hard to supervise, and frequent style changes can cause timbre drift.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.951
Our key idea is to separate contextual style decisions from their acoustic realization.

00:00:40.111 --> 00:00:43.934
An executable style instruction connects perception and expression.

00:00:45.344 --> 00:00:50.781
At each turn, Context-to-Instruction receives the interaction history and the target text.

00:00:50.941 --> 00:00:57.302
The speech generator uses that text, the predicted instruction, and a persistent reference-speaker prompt.

00:00:58.712 --> 00:01:05.946
C2I learns from rationale supervision and on-policy self-distillation, helping it interpret sparse multimodal cues.

00:01:06.106 --> 00:01:09.732
Only the final style instruction is passed to the speech generator.

00:01:11.142 --> 00:01:17.938
Iterative rejection sampling selects generated candidates that better follow the instruction and preserve speaker identity.

00:01:18.098 --> 00:01:23.547
Context-aware DPO then learns which valid realization best fits the original interaction.

00:01:25.492 --> 00:01:30.372
File three is in the second drawer on your left.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:37.212
I'm so happy for you! You deserve this. Celebrate!

00:01:38.992 --> 00:01:45.952
Failing once doesn't mean you're useless. You've worked hard; let's work out what to adjust next time.

00:01:47.342 --> 00:01:55.484
Interactive TTS. Explicit style decisions, contextually appropriate expression, and a consistent speaker across turns.
